{
  "id": "Compound::DB01124 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Tolbutamide is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular interactions involving cytochrome P450 enzymes. The evidence suggests that Tolbutamide binds to Cyp2c9 and Cyp2c8, which in turn participate in the oxidation of arachidonic acid and limonene, both of which are substrates of Cyp2c19. This indicates a potential pathway where Tolbutamide may influence Cyp2c19 through the modulation of its substrate specificity. The shared involvement of Cyp2c9 and Cyp2c8 in the oxidation of different substrates suggests a possible functional overlap or regulatory interaction between these enzymes. The cumulative evidence points to a mechanism where Tolbutamide could indirectly affect Cyp2c19 by altering the activity of its substrates, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
